      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-05-29_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>EXAMINER Series</head>
        <p>THE EXAMINER Series</p>
        <p>OF WEEK-END NEWSPAPERS COMPRISES : TE WARRINGTON EXAMINER, published every H Saturday morning, principal and the Oldest Weekly Paper for Warrington,Stockton Heath,Penketh,Winwick, Padgate, Lymm, being.. one of the Largest and Best Weekly Papers in Lancashire and Cheshire. The district covered by this Paper comprises a large trading and agricultural tract in South Lancashire and Mid- Cheshire. --- - -</p>
        <p>T---------- HE RUNCORN EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. It is the best weekly paper in the Town and District, and offers the best and cheapest facilities to Advertisers. MHE WIDNES EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. Widnes contains the largest number of chemical works of any town in the Kingdom, and is a rapidly growing centre of industry. THDEARLESTOWN AND NEWTON EXAMINER published every Saturday morning. The Largest Local Paper containing _ the News of Earlestown, Newton-le-Willows, Golborne, Haydock, Lowton, &amp;c. The district thus comprised is a most important part of the Lancashire coalfields. MA ST. HELENS EXAMINER, published every i Saturday morning, circulating n St. Helens, Prescot, Parr Sutton, Peasley Cross &amp;c.—the centre of the Glass, Chemical,and Watch Trades of the Kingdom,</p>
