        <p>Fit 0 43 0 ve4,41,_.P n Sweepstakes. (Any .Rifle). units 31n. bull's eye: Possible 35. ii• D. Ga il'pier I% ~,.. _ r 1., %-,,,,tiennion —. Y. VBo y - er 28. A. VVarburt C• 13- Day °n 27 A, Down 27 f1,,,,14 1144 ilowarl . - c )4447, p. °laresie an tt t ion Messrs. F. C. Bennion. C. W. d dAWarburton tied for second liktittaial IL re-hootproved Mr. Bennion to be the P' Members' Stakes. (Any Rifle). A m. Ant_ ; Gin, bull's eye ; five shots, disappearing 'otsibie 40. -• NV. Plin t 39 C F. vrar .t." . S on 38 P. . p. iP. Girdiuer 38 1 Varo %_. iurton I. 13 tT 39 n • ougliton 35 • P. .4. , ey 33 ~.._ cowi BelMio •(.3. w. 13 u 32 ll' p. 011°37 17" 3L ,%. ~. ard _ 4..0 ward VorhbolBtaljti "1.8 3o' 'alll-43 -es oily rifle) seven shots fin bull's eye. the .34. Who \ Reuther .. A tried, t, er this competition was 141 r. A. B. Mellor, it`th_epecitoup creditable score of 32 points. -`glth it Lean). Will visit St. Helens to-day, to shoot githist the St.. Helens Civilian Rifle Club.</p>
        <p>The National Memorial to Victoria the Good, which is nearing completion, was partially nnveiled to the public on Monday. The monument stands at the base of the Royal road in St. James's Park where it forms an oasis of cool marble in the broad avenue that stretches !ronl Buckingham Palace to the Admiralty; and although it will not be completed in all Its essentials until the end of 1910, it is already an object of great interest. The arrange. Mieut of Ihe gushing fountains is a work of great engineering skill. Over a million gallons (21 water a day pour out of the bronze and marble mouths into the basins, and from there 143 the lake in St. James's Park from which it is partially drawn.</p>
        <p>A great demonstration was held in London on Monday to celebrate Empire Day, :rards of 5,000 children marchin, in procession from the Embankment to Hyde Park, ere a simple and impressive ceremony was carried out. The flag of the Empire ;uttered on a 60 ft. staff, and in fours the youngsters of the League of the Empire, the 17 League, Baden Powell's Scouts, and Lord Roberts' Boys saluted it as they passed with ;se Precision of military veterans. Earl of Meath and Earl Roberts were interested recfators of the demonstration.</p>
