        <head>Examiner, Saturday, May 29, 1909 METHODISM kT BROOM EDGE.</head>
        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, May 29, 1909 METHODISM kT BROOM EDGE.</p>
        <p>insurance of the members of the brigade against risk. It had also decided that operation should be limited to Stockton Heath, but if 'required the Brigade could go to Latchford Without and Walton Inferior at the usual rates. This um carried. - THE VOTERS' LIST. Mr. Westbrook said the assistant-overseer had asked him to sal that the revision of the voters' list would be , held in July and he asked that there should be a revision of the numbers in Walton-road. At present there were two numbered 36 and also one nurnLr3red 36A in Walton-road. They ought to be attended to. In IVhitefield-road there were houses that were not numbered, and in Derby-road they were not numbered at all. The speaker proposed that the whole of tbe village be - examined and the numbers put right where Wrong. This was carried.</p>
