      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-05-29_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>King's Visit,</head>
        <p>The King's Visit,</p>
        <p>B.r,—With regard to the suggession as to the -window-box decoration, the Executive Committee of this Society are entirely in accord with it, and desire to assist in every possible way. It is therefore proposed to arrange for the supply of window boxes through the Society at the cheapest price possible. This price will somewhat depend upon the number of boxes ordered, and I shall be glad if those who are prepared to secure boxes will send me a postcard, so that an idea of the number required may be obtained. —Yours truly, _</p>
        <p>GEORGE H. SMITH, Secretary Beautiful Warrington Society, The Old Academy,, Bridge-street, Warrington, 27th May, 1009. •</p>
